Overlay patch 0013: game-state exports the iOS shell links against.

The shared shell (app/ios/SohIosShell.m) declares seven externs the GAME must
provide. They are what let the touch layer behave correctly without the shell
ever reading game memory itself:

    SohIos_IsMenuOpen      -> auto-hide the touch overlay while a menu is up
    SohIos_IsPopupOpen     -> yield ALL touches while an ImGui popup is open
                              (fixed-stick zones AND floating-stick regions
                              both ate popup buttons on real fingers)
    SohIos_IsGamePaused    -> show the menu chip while paused
    SohIos_IsTitleOrDemo   -> show the menu chip at title/demo, hide it in play
    SohIos_ActiveSeqIds    -> music diagnostic over the console bridge
    SohIos_QueueMenuScroll -> mouse-free menu scrolling (consumed by 0018)
    SohIos_HasEnteredGameplay -> keep the menu chip alive through boot/intro
    SohIos_IsIntroPlaying     -> hide the touch layer over the intro video

BK-specific mappings (this is where the port diverges from SoH, whose
pauseCtx/gPlayState globals do not exist here — Lighthouse's own menu code
still carries "TODO" stubs where gPlayState would go):

    paused      = getGameMode() == GAME_MODE_4_PAUSED
    title/demo  = GAME_MODE_7_ATTRACT_DEMO or GAME_MODE_9_BANJO_AND_KAZOOIE
                  (the attract demo and the title/logo mode)
    menu open   = Ship::Context Gui::GetMenuOrMenubarVisible()
    popup open  = ImGui::IsPopupOpen(nullptr, ImGuiPopupFlags_AnyPopup)

Two are deliberately staged rather than faked:
  * SohIos_HudStats is NOT here — overlay 0008 (the perf probe) owns it, since
    it is the thing that actually has the number. 0013 briefly carried a 0.0f
    stub while 0008 was pending; that stub is gone rather than left to collide.
  * SohIos_QueueMenuScroll accumulates here; patch 0018 applies the queued
    (x, dy) via ImGui::SetScrollY inside each scrollable BeginChild. Wheel
    injection is a known dead end (tooltips + slider jumps), so the queue is
    the interface between the two patches.

Match-count asserted against the pristine vendor state.

--- a/src/port/Engine.cpp
+++ b/src/port/Engine.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 #include "Engine.h"
+#include "port/UI/LighthouseGui.hpp"
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <filesystem>
 #include <fstream>
@@ -1666,5 +1667,84 @@
             MemoryPool.erase(it);
             break;
         }
+    }
+}
+
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// LIGHTHOUSE_IOS (overlay 0013): game-state exports for the iOS app shell.
+// File-scope extern "C" on purpose — a block-scope linkage spec does not
+// compile in C++, and block-scope externs namespace-mangle (both cost the
+// flagship a debugging session). The shell never reads game memory; it asks
+// these questions and gets a plain int back.
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+extern "C" {
+
+int SohIos_IsMenuOpen(void) {
+    auto ctx = Ship::Context::GetRawInstance();
+    if (ctx == nullptr) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    auto gui = ctx->GetWindow() != nullptr ? ctx->GetWindow()->GetGui() : nullptr;
+    return (gui != nullptr && gui->GetMenuOrMenubarVisible()) ? 1 : 0;
+}
+
+int SohIos_IsPopupOpen(void) {
+    return ImGui::IsPopupOpen(nullptr, ImGuiPopupFlags_AnyPopup) ? 1 : 0;
+}
+
+int SohIos_IsGamePaused(void) {
+    return getGameMode() == GAME_MODE_4_PAUSED ? 1 : 0;
+}
+
+int SohIos_IsTitleOrDemo(void) {
+    const s32 mode = getGameMode();
+    return (mode == GAME_MODE_7_ATTRACT_DEMO || mode == GAME_MODE_9_BANJO_AND_KAZOOIE) ? 1 : 0;
+}
+
+// Has the player reached actual gameplay yet? STICKY: once BK reaches
+// GAME_MODE_3_NORMAL it stays true for the session. The shell uses it to keep
+// the menu chip visible through boot logos, intro and file-select — none of
+// which are "paused" or "title/demo", so the chip used to vanish exactly when a
+// new user needed it (user report, device, 2026-07-31).
+static bool sLhEnteredGameplay = false;
+
+int SohIos_HasEnteredGameplay(void) {
+    if (!sLhEnteredGameplay && getGameMode() == GAME_MODE_3_NORMAL) {
+        sLhEnteredGameplay = true;
     }
+    return sLhEnteredGameplay ? 1 : 0;
 }
+
+// Is the non-interactive boot-logo / intro sequence on screen? BK's pre-title
+// modes are 1 and 2 (the decomp still calls them UNKNOWN). Reported in the perf
+// line as `mode=` so this heuristic can be checked on a device rather than
+// assumed — if the intro turns out to use another mode, widen it there.
+// Used to hide the touch layer over a video that takes no input.
+int SohIos_IsIntroPlaying(void) {
+    if (SohIos_HasEnteredGameplay()) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    const s32 mode = getGameMode();
+    return (mode == GAME_MODE_1_UNKNOWN || mode == GAME_MODE_2_UNKNOWN) ? 1 : 0;
+}
+
+// Music diagnostic for the console bridge. BK's sequence player does not expose
+// a SoH-style active-sequence bitfield; wired to 0 until the audio work maps
+// one, so `seq` over the bridge answers honestly instead of guessing.
+uint32_t SohIos_ActiveSeqIds(void) {
+    return 0;
+}
+
+// Mouse-free menu scrolling. The shell queues a finger-x-targeted (x, dy);
+// overlay 0018 drains it inside each scrollable BeginChild via ImGui::SetScrollY.
+// Injecting wheel events instead is a dead end: it fires tooltips and makes
+// sliders jump.
+float gSohIosScrollX = 0.0f;
+float gSohIosScrollDy = 0.0f;
+
+void SohIos_QueueMenuScroll(float x, float dy) {
+    gSohIosScrollX = x;
+    gSohIosScrollDy += dy;
+}
+
+} // extern "C"
